      "id": 1,
      "text": "East Liverpool earned the nickname “Ceramic City” because its pottery industry once dominated the U.S. market.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Liverpool%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The downtown historic district spans 22 acres and showcases Italianate and Second Empire buildings that once housed the city’s thriving commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Liverpool%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1893, Moorish‑ and Persian‑influenced pottery from East Liverpool won awards at the Chicago World’s Columbian Exposition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Liverpool%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city’s Carnegie library, opened in 1902, was the first of Ohio’s Carnegie libraries and remains a landmark of early 20th‑century architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Liverpool%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "East Liverpool sits on the Ohio River where the borders of Ohio, Pennsylvania, and West Virginia meet, about 30 miles from Pittsburgh.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Liverpool%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Lewis and Clark National Historic Trail, commemorating the 1804–06 expedition, passes through East Liverpool, linking the town to a national legacy.",
